Krita Nova 84 - Shortcut Composer bundled as a built-in Python plugin

Shortcut Composer 1.7.1 by Wojciech Trybus (GPL-3.0-or-later,
https://github.com/wojtryb/Shortcut-Composer, commit e3fe151): pie menus,
cursor trackers, multiple assignments, temporary keys and rotation
selectors bound to keyboard shortcuts.

- plugins/python/shortcut_composer: the plugin, its manual and license;
  its action file is installed as krita/actions/shortcut_composer.action
- it is enabled by default (kritarc [python] enable_shortcut_composer
  still switches it off)
- its startup warning about OpenGL on Windows with Krita 6 is for Qt 6
  builds only; it is skipped on Krita Nova's Qt 5 build

Needs Krita's Python scripting: the Windows build has it; the Android
build has no PyQt, so the plugin is not loaded there.

diff --git a/plugins/extensions/pykrita/plugin/PythonPluginManager.cpp b/plugins/extensions/pykrita/plugin/PythonPluginManager.cpp
index 749f50a..a587827 100644
--- a/plugins/extensions/pykrita/plugin/PythonPluginManager.cpp
+++ b/plugins/extensions/pykrita/plugin/PythonPluginManager.cpp
@@ -320,7 +320,9 @@ void PythonPluginManager::scanPlugins()
 
             verifyDependenciesSetStatus(plugin);
 
-            plugin.m_enabled = pluginSettings.readEntry(QString("enable_") + plugin.moduleName(), false);
+            // Krita Nova: the bundled Shortcut Composer is on unless switched off
+            const bool enabledByDefault = plugin.moduleName() == "shortcut_composer";
+            plugin.m_enabled = pluginSettings.readEntry(QString("enable_") + plugin.moduleName(), enabledByDefault);
 
             m_plugins.append(plugin);
         }
